# Performance Guidelines

## React Rendering

- Use `useMemo` for expensive derived data (see dashboard stats calculation)
- Use `useCallback` sparingly — only when passing to memoized children
- Avoid creating objects/arrays inline in JSX props when they cause re-renders
- Keep component trees shallow — extract only when reused

## Data Fetching

React Query configuration patterns from the codebase:

```typescript
// Standard query
useQuery({ queryKey: ["gardens"], queryFn: fetchGardens });

// Cached with staleTime (weather)
useQuery({
  queryKey: ["weather", lat, lon],
  staleTime: CACHE_TTL,        // 30 minutes
  refetchOnWindowFocus: false,
  initialData: cached?.data,
});
```

- Set appropriate `staleTime` to reduce refetches
- Disable `refetchOnWindowFocus` for stable data (weather)
- Invalidate queries after mutations, not refetch everything

## Code Splitting

- TanStack Router handles route-level splitting automatically
- Lazy load heavy components only when needed (e.g. xlsx in reports)
- Do not import large libraries at module top level if used conditionally

## Caching

- Weather: localStorage with TTL (`use-weather.ts`)
- Location: localStorage persistence (`farm-weather-location`)
- AI reports: database persistence (`ai_reports` table)

## Images

- Disease diagnosis currently uses data URLs — consider Supabase Storage for production
- Use appropriate image sizes before upload
- Do not store unnecessarily large base64 strings

## Network

- Batch Supabase reads where possible (`Promise.all` in server functions)
- Limit query results (e.g. logs limited to 500 in AI context)
- Weather API: coordinate rounding to reduce cache key proliferation

## Do Not

- Prematurely optimize with complex abstractions
- Add caching libraries — use React Query + localStorage
- Block UI rendering for non-critical data
